565786 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566191 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186565935 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566191 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186565952 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566191 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566191 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566191 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186565786 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566191 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f9154569-4f80-5022-95a7-7098388b2e9a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566198 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186566157 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566198 #edb/ref 1069 "q-123512" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566198 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566198 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[4,5]\\times [2,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=8x-2y-1.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566198 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "00814162-4a3c-58fe-a969-f047df1ff44b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566198 #edb/ref 1074 "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=8x-2y-1$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=8x-2y-1$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/01/01b291ca7cd81b88cf6ed06fdcdb2ffcbb1f78255d0f57d496823d347c2fb0b3.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/a4/a44c2586978022663635d1f35399166c1ae32963fe0f4bffebd21966ad40bac5.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j})=8{x}_{i-1}-2{y}_{j}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}_{(}f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(8{x}_{i-1}-2{y}_{j}-1)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $8{x}_{i-1}-2{y}_{j}-1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566218 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186566138 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566218 #edb/ref 1069 "q-164124" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566218 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566218 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[0,1]\\times [1,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+2x.$ \nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566218 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2f8d79c3-b613-54e6-b2e9-de270331920a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566218 #edb/ref 1074 "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+2x$ increases as $x$ increases on $[0,1]$, and\n\n- $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+2x$ increases as $y$ increases on $[1,2].$\n\n![](images/67/67daa328cc6ae4cb37be386c327fb4548844fad2adc10476bdf1147c5a5d4218.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/51/51808df96cf7dd295bfa24aa3641a601c821116e1a0014898ffe705036704a53.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j-1})={x}_{i-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}^{2}+2{x}_{i-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}^{2}+2{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is ${x}_{i-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}^{2}+2{x}_{i-1}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566230 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186566191 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566230 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75327" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566230 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566230 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[1,3]\\times [3,4]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=140-4{x}^{2}-6{y}^{2}.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566230 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "577873fb-8648-59ce-9de9-8ad820b016f9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566230 #edb/ref 1074 "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=140-4{x}^{2}-6{y}^{2}$ decreases as $x$ increases on $[1,3]$, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=140-4{x}^{2}-6{y}^{2}$ decreases as $y$ increases on $[3,4].$\n\n![](images/ce/ce0d90127e1f14654f4b32a933f1eb6e76e054c03f19ca40c3f04116aa3c2c93.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/4a/4a10c8332a5f346d393c37531c13db6aa69d4cecb241efd7c34d57f32d5a98b8.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j})=140-4{x}_{i}^{2}-6{y}_{j}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(140-4{x}_{i}^{2}-6{y}_{j}^{2})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $140-4{x}_{i}^{2}-6{y}_{j}^{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566233 #edb/ref 1068 